<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Changing the Subject 2 - Area of a trapezium</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The area of a trapezium is given by \(A = \frac{1}{2}(a+b)h\).</p>
<p>(a) Make \(h\) the subject of the formula.</p>
<p>\(h = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) A trapezium has area \({@nA@}\ \text{cm}^2\) and parallel sides of length \({@na@}\ \text{cm}\) and \({@nb@}\ \text{cm}\). Use your formula to find its height \(h\) in cm.</p>
<p>\(h = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Multiply both sides by 2: \(2A = (a+b)h\).</p>
<p>Divide both sides by \((a+b)\): \(h = \frac{2A}{a+b}\).</p>
<p>Substituting: \(h = \frac{2({@nA@})}{ {@na@} + {@nb@} } = {@nh@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
